C runtime / SDK headers the NT DDKs include but don't ship, reduced to what their
#includes need for types to compile (tools/legacy/headers.py). Not Microsoft's text.
  ctype.h, string.h: wchar_t / size_t       stddef.h, stdarg.h: empty
  excpt.h: EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION as int (an enum of int size in the real header)
  pshpackN.h / poppack.h: #pragma pack(push,N) / (pop), their whole effect
  alphaops.h: empty (Alpha instruction encodings; no kernel type uses it)
